<section style="padding:96px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>A fibreglass oil tank in Newfoundland is the closest thing to a buy-it-once purchase a homeowner can make for their heating system. Under the province's heating oil tank rules, a steel tank gets a tag good for 10 to 25 years depending on how it's built. A fibreglass or double-wall tank gets a service life set by the administrator instead, and that can run as long as 50 years. We've seen fibreglass tags stamped out to 2061.</p><p>Harbour Tank Co installs fibreglass and Roth double-wall tanks across St. John's and the Avalon, from Mount Pearl and Paradise out to Conception Bay South, Torbay and Bay Roberts. The upgrade runs about $650 more than a steel tank, roughly $3,850 installed against $3,200, and it buys two to three times the service life. Every job starts with a free written estimate, and we're licensed and insured. Call (709) 800-3117 or read on to see whether the upgrade makes sense for your house.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Tags that can run to 50 years</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Steel tanks top out at 10 to 25 years under section 15(1) of the province's tank regulations. Fibreglass and double-wall tanks get a life set by the administrator under section 15(5), capped at 50 years.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">About $650 more than steel</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A fibreglass tank runs about $3,850 installed against $3,200 for steel. That extra $650 buys two to three times the service life, so it's cheaper per year of heat.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Roth double-wall for indoors</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">For basement and utility-room installs we fit Roth double-containment tanks, a plastic inner tank inside a galvanized steel outer shell. If the inner tank ever weeps, the outer shell holds it.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">No rust in salt air</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Steel tanks on the Avalon coast lose years to salt air, especially in Torbay, Portugal Cove-St. Philip's and around Conception Bay. Fibreglass doesn't corrode, so an outdoor tank near the water keeps its full life.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">100-gallon tanks for heat-pump homes</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">If oil is only your backup heat, you don't need a full-size tank. A 100-gallon tank installs for about $3,100 and still gets the long fibreglass tag.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Free written estimates, licensed and insured</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">You get a price in writing before any work starts, and we can haul the old tank away as part of the same job. If your tag has already expired and the truck won't fill you, the same number answers 24/7: (709) 800-3117.</p>
      </div>
</div>
